  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "summon companion to fight alongside",
    "skill1": "convert enemy HP-loss into a personal shield",
    "skill2": "share a portion of received shield with bonded ally",
    "skill3": "damage reduction grows while shielded",
    "skill4": "companion frightens nearby enemies",
    "skill5": "excess shield value converts to HP"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Daimon]] fights with an untargetable companion that frightens nearby enemies and joins his ultimate for true damage based on enemy HP. The companion attacks at battle start, while [[Daimon]] converts enemy HP-loss into a personal shield and shares part of it with a bonded ally. He gains damage reduction while shielded, and excess shield value converts to HP. He blends tanking, shielding, and sub-DPS in one slot. Without frequent shield generation, a healer, or HP-loss triggers, his sustain loop is much weaker.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Daimon]] turns enemy HP-loss and companion hits into personal shields, shares shield with a bonded ally, and gains damage reduction while shielded; the companion is untargetable. Delete [[Daimon]] early with high-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Shakir]] before shields stack, or delay the bonded partner with [[filter:backline-inhibit]] like [[Bonnie]] or [[Evie]]. Once the shield cycle is online, use lasting coverage like [[Gwyneth]] or [[Shemira]] rather than trying to kill the companion. Denying HP-loss triggers also starves his sustain."
}
